//? Title: Regularised Tree Boosting for Iris: Fit, Select, Then Test
//? Subtitle: Diagonal Newton updates, validation loss paths and a separate final test set
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
We derive the regularised leaf weights and split gains used by datamunge's
XGBoost-style multiclass classifier. The implementation uses one class tree
per round and a diagonal softmax curvature approximation; it is not a
binding to the upstream XGBoost system. Fisher's iris measurements are split
into training, validation and test partitions. Fixed-model staged evaluation
separates decreasing training loss from validation behaviour, and a
validation-only search selects the L2 penalty and round count. A model
refitted on all development data is then evaluated once on the reserved
test partition using accuracy, mean log loss, Brier score and class counts.
)

\toc

> The data and the evaluation design

`dm::datasets::iris()` has 150 flowers, four measurements in centimetres,
and three string-valued species labels with 50 observations each. Petal
measurements show clear setosa separation and an overlap between the other
two species. The classifier uses all four measurements, without scaling;
a two-dimensional scatter is descriptive, not the full decision space.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/xgb_iris_data.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const auto iris = dm::datasets::iris();
  std::print("{}\n",iris.head(6).to_md());
  std::print("\n{}\n",(iris | dm::group_by("Species") | dm::summarise(dm::agg::n("flowers"),
      dm::agg::mean("Petal.Length","mean_petal_length"),dm::agg::mean("Petal.Width","mean_petal_width"))).to_md(3));
  const auto [development,test] = dm::stats::train_test_split(iris,0.2,42,"Species");
  const auto [train,validation] = dm::stats::train_test_split(development,0.25,43,"Species");
  std::print("\n| partition | flowers | flowers per species |\n| :--- | ---: | ---: |\n"
      "| training | {} | 30 |\n| validation | {} | 10 |\n| final test | {} | 10 |\n",train.nrows(),validation.nrows(),test.nrows());
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  dm::graphics::GGPlot::create(iris,{"Petal.Length","Petal.Width","Species","",""}).geom_point()
      .labs("Iris petal measurements","petal length (cm)","petal width (cm)")
      .theme_minimal().save_svg("build/xgb_iris_data.svg");
}
```
